   "file": "TauCeti/Algebra/Star/Subalgebra.lean",
   "fix": "Add `Subalgebra.mul_toSubmodule_of_commute (S T : Subalgebra R A) (h : \u2200 a \u2208 S, \u2200 b \u2208 T, Commute a b) : toSubmodule S * toSubmodule T = toSubmodule (S \u2294 T)` with `[Semiring A]`. Then derive the `StarSubalgebra` version from it, noting that the `Subalgebra` join of star-closed `S` and `T` is star-closed, so it equals `(S \u2294 T).toSubalgebra`.",
   "issue": "`StarSubalgebra.toSubmodule_sup_of_commute` re-proves by hand that `S.toSubmodule * T.toSubmodule` is a subalgebra containing `S` and `T`. The star structure only enters through `star_mem'`. The natural general result is the noncommutative, elementwise-commuting version of Mathlib's `Subalgebra.mul_toSubmodule`, which currently requires `[CommSemiring A]`.",
